{"type":"say","text":"Great, I'm glad we're all on the same page. Lina, I'll bring the tapes to Theo's apartment on Saturday afternoon — that keeps the chain of custody simple since I have the box right now. Before Saturday, the three of us should go through the tapes together to assess which ones are deteriorating fastest and agree on a priority order, like you said. Maybe we could do that Thursday or Friday evening?

As for the digital files, a shared family folder with restricted access sounds like a good approach. We'll need to finalize the list of Aaron's descendants before granting anyone access, and we should make sure the folder is secure.

So to summarize where we stand: Saturday afternoon transfer at Theo's with the calibrated deck, prioritizing the most deteriorated tapes first. Originals go to Lina's cabinet afterward. Digital copies shared only with Aaron's descendants via a restricted family folder. Does anyone have any other concerns, or are we ready to move forward with this plan?"}

